hadiths[215]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10201","112 / 89 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Asbagh narrated to us from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gecko is a devil. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with an isnad except Yunus. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
"10202","113 / 90 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Asbagh narrated to us from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10203","114 / 91 - And from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cutting is for a quarter dinar and above. And we do not know anyone who combined Urwah and Amrah except Yunus. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
"10204","115 / 92 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Anbasah narrated to us from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: He used to say in his illness - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Aishah, I have never ceased to feel the pain of the food I ate at Khaybar; now is the time I feel my aorta being cut from that poison. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yunus except Anbasah. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
"10205","116 / 93 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us from Anbasah, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night, and a prostration therein was for as long as one of you recites fifty verses. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yunus except Anbasah. Ahmad narrated to us, he said:"
"10206","117 / 94 - Nahshal ibn Kathir al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some poetry is wisdom."
"10207","118 / 95 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us from Zam'ah, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some poetry is wisdom. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with an isnad from Ibn Uyaynah except Nahshal ibn Kathir and Khalid ibn Nizar. And it is known from Zam'ah."
"10208","119 / 96 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah: from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven rak'ahs in the night, greeting in every two prostrations (rak'ahs), and witr with one."
"10209","120 / 97 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer, and the women and children slept. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: The women and children have slept, while you await the prayer."
"10210","121 / 98 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted Ashura and commanded fasting it."
"10211","122 / 99 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting the day of Ashura, the tenth day. And we do not know anyone who narrated this wording except Abu Asim from Ibn Abi Dhi'b."
"10212","123 / 100 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Faraj and Umar ibn Sa'id narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the believer falls ill, Allah purifies him just as the bellows purifies the dross of iron. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Ibn Abi Dhi'b. And there is disagreement over Ibn Abi Dhi'b: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, while other than Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah."
"10213","124 / 101 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah that she said: Abu Bakr sought permission upon us while two slave girls were singing with me and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lay on his bed; so Abu Bakr rebuked me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered his face and said: Leave them, for they are days of Eid."
"10214","125 / 102 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: A physiognomist entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Usamah and Zayd lay down, and said: These feet are some from others. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pleased with that and it delighted him."
"10215","126 / 103 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven rak'ahs, making witr of them with one; when he finished he lay on his right side."
"10216","127 / 104 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah with a single tawaf, while those who entered ihram for Umrah circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah after they returned from Mina."
"10217","128 / 105 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah who said: I asked Aishah about the saying of Allah, blessed and exalted: {Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah; whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no blame upon him to circumambulate them}. I said: By Allah, there is no blame upon anyone for not circumambulating them. She said: Evil is what you said, O son of my sister; if it were as you interpreted it, it would read: there is no blame upon him for not circumambulating them. But it was only revealed - and the Ansar before they became Muslim used to enter ihram for Manat, the idol they worshipped near the House, and whoever circumambulated her felt scruple about circumambulating al-Safa and al-Marwah - so when they became Muslim they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that and said: O Messenger of Allah, we feel scruple about circumambulating al-Safa and al-Marwah. So Allah, mighty and exalted, revealed: {Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah; whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no blame upon him to circumambulate them}. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established the tawaf of them as sunnah, so no one should leave tawaf of them. And we do not know a better presentation of this hadith than al-Zuhri's, from Urwah."
"10218","129 / 106 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Zubaydi narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will gather people barefoot, naked, uncircumcised. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah except al-Zubaydi."
"10219","130 / 107 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muhammad narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Apply kohl with ithmid, for it clears the sight and fixes the hair - or: the hair. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah except al-Walid ibn Muhammad, and he is weak in hadith, known as al-Muwaqqari."
"10220","131 / 108 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Isma'il narrated to us from Umar ibn Surayj, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah except Umar ibn Surayj, and most scholars disagreed with this narration. And Umar ibn Surayj is Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Surayj; he narrated from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il and Fudayl ibn Sulayman and others."
"10221","132 / 109 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah - meaning Ibn Salih - narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Servants are Allah's servants, and lands are Allah's lands; whoever revives something of dead land, it is his, and the unjust root has no right. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah except Zam'ah."
"10222","133 / 110 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mu'ammal al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Abi Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I had two gold bracelets, and said: Shall I not point you to what is better for you than this and finer? I said: Yes. He said: Make them of silver, then perfume them so they look like gold. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10223","134 / 111 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given a favor and mentions it has thanked for it, and whoever feigns satiety with what he was not given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar. And Salih is weak in hadith, though many scholars narrated from him."
"10224","135 / 112 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Musa, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman married without her guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void, her marriage is void; if he consummates with her, she has her dowry for what he attained of her; if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"10225","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 136 / 113 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it. And this hadith was narrated by Sulayman ibn Musa, Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, all from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10226","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 137 / 114 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us from Usamah ibn Zayd, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10227","138 / 114 (m) - Usamah said: And Hafs ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the prayer of the hypocrite? He leaves Asr until when it is between the two horns of Satan - or: upon the two horns of Satan - he stands and pecks them like the pecking of a rooster, remembering Allah in them only little. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Usamah ibn Zayd, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10228","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 139 / 115 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Nafi', from Usamah ibn Zayd, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was passed by Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith, and he said: O Aishah, come so I may show you my cousin who satirized me. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Usamah, nor from Usamah except Abdullah ibn Nafi'."
"10229","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 140 / 116 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us from Ibn Abi Uways - meaning Abu Bakr - from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When revelation came to me - or: I was given prophethood, or a word like it - I would not pass by a stone or a tree except that it said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yahya ibn Sa'id, nor do we know a path for it except this path."
"10230","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 141 / 117 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands Ramadan in faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibrahim ibn Isma'il, and Ja'far ibn Awn and Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated it from Ibrahim."
"10231","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 142 / 118 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Wathiq narrated to us, he said: Abu Abbad narrated to us - a shaykh from the people of Madinah - from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jabir: Shall I not give you glad tidings? He said: May Allah give you good tidings of good. He said: Do you know that Allah gave life to your father and said: My servant, wish for whatever you will of Me, I shall give it to you? He said: So he said: O Lord, I wish of You that You return me so I am killed once more. He said: It has already preceded from Me that to it you shall not return. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aishah except from this angle, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri except Abu Abbad, and Abu Abbad was narrated from by Abu Dawud, al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam and al-Fadl ibn Wathiq."
"10232","143 / 119 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: Umm Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth; a woman sees in her dream what a man sees - should she wash? He said: Yes."
"10233","144 / 120 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us from al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it. Aishah said: So I said to her: Does a woman see that? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to her and said: May your right hand be dusty; whence is resemblance? And this hadith was narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, while Hisham ibn Urwah differed therein, narrating it from his father, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10234","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 145 / 121 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10235","146 / 122 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Humayd narrated to us from Salih, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10236","147 / 123 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us from al-Umari, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: I woke up, I and Hafsah, fasting, then food was gifted to us - and food was dear in those days - so we broke our fast, then we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Fast a day in its place."
"10237","148 / 124 - And Khallad ibn Aslam narrated it to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah and Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri mursal, while those we named narrated it with an isnad."
"10238","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 149 / 125 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Anbasah narrated to us from Amr ibn Maymun, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, marfu': that he forbade cutting dates from palms at night. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aishah except from this angle, and Anbasah is weak in hadith; he narrated hadiths in which he was not corroborated."
"10239","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 150 / 126 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: I used to rub janabah off the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Aishah, except Ja'far ibn Burqan."
"10240","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 151 / 127 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abu Qatadah al-Adawi narrated to us from Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah and Asma that they said: Our mother came to us in Madinah while she was a polytheist, during the truce between Quraysh and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So we said: O Messenger of Allah, our mother has come to us desirous; shall we maintain ties with her? He said: Yes, maintain ties with her. And we do not know this hadith narrated from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah and Asma, except from this angle."
"10241","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 152 / 128 - Idris ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Were it not that I would impose hardship on my ummah, I would command them to use the siwak at every prayer. And this hadith was narrated by the memorizers from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurairah, and we do not know anyone who corroborated Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya in his narration; we already mentioned Mu'awiyah's weakness in hadith."
"10242","153 / 129 - I heard Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna saying: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us - he said: And he read it to me from his book - he said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us from al-Zuhri who said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, Alqamah ibn Waqqas and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah concerning the hadith of Aishah when the people of ifk said of her what they said, and Allah declared her innocent of what they said; each narrated to me a portion of the hadith which these narrated to me from Aishah, some confirming others, though some were more retentive than others. They claimed: that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go out, he would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out with her. Aishah said: So he cast lots among us in a campaign he fought, and I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Allah revealed the hijab; I would descend and be carried in my howdah. We marched until, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished that campaign of his and returned, and we drew near Madinah returning, he announced departure one night. So I stood until the army passed, and when I finished I came to my riding place and found a necklace of mine of onyx beads had broken, so I returned seeking my necklace, and seeking it detained me. The group who used to saddle my camel which I rode came, thinking I was in it - women in those days were light, not carrying flesh; we ate only a morsel of food - so the people did not notice the lightness of the howdah, and I was a young girl. I found my necklace after the army had gone on, then I came to their camping places with neither caller nor answerer in them, and I thought they would miss me and return to me. While I sat in my place, my eyes overcame me and I slept. Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal al-Sulami was among those behind the army; he saw a black shape, came to me, and recognized me when he saw me - he had seen me before the hijab - so I woke at his istirja' when he recognized me. By Allah, I heard no word from him other than his istirja', until he made his camel kneel, stepped on its neck, and I rode it; he took the camel's head leading me until we reached the army after they had camped, and those who perished perished. Then I came to Madinah and fell ill when I arrived for a month, while people spread talk about me and I sensed nothing of that; what puzzled me in my sickness was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I used to see before - he would only enter upon me, greet, then say: How is this one? And I sensed nothing, until I went out after I recovered, going out with Umm Mistah toward al-Manasi' - we went out only at night, before latrines were taken, our affair being the affair of the first Arabs. So I went out, I and Umm Mistah - she is the daughter of Abi Ruhm ibn Abd Manaf, and her son is Mistah ibn Uthathah - and Umm Mistah stumbled in her cloak and said: May Mistah perish. I said: Evil is what you say! Do you revile a man who witnessed Badr?! She said: O dear, have you not heard what he said? I said: What is that? She said: She told me the saying of the people of ifk, so my sickness increased upon my sickness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and said: How is this one? I said: Will you permit me to go to my parents? - I then wanted to seek news from them. She said: So he permitted me, and I came to my parents and said to my mother: O dear, what are people saying? She said: O my daughter, take it easy; by Allah, seldom was there ever a beautiful woman with a man who loves her, having co-wives, except that they spoke much against her. I said: Glory be to Allah, have people spoken of this? She said: So I wept that night until morning, my tears never stopping nor sleeping with sleep, and I awoke weeping. The Messenger of Allah called Ali and Usamah - I said: consulting them about his family. As for Usamah, he advised the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with what he knew of his family's innocence and what he knew in himself for them, saying: O Messenger of Allah, your family, and we know only good. As for Ali, he said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not constrained you, and women besides her are many; if you ask the slave girl, she will tell you the truth. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Barirah and said to her: O Barirah, have you seen any doubt - or: anything? - or a word like it. She said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I never saw anything in her I could fault - or another word, Abu Muhammad doubted - upon her, more than that she is a young girl who sleeps over her family's dough so the domestic goat comes and eats it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood after that day seeking excuse from Abdullah ibn Ubayy; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Muslims, who will excuse me concerning a man whose harm reached my family? By Allah, I know of my family only good, and they mentioned a man of whom I know only good, and he would not enter upon my family except with me. So Sa'd ibn Mu'adh stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I excuse you from him; if he is from Aws, we strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers Khazraj, command us and we carry out your command. She said: So Sa'd ibn Ubadah stood - he was the chief of Khazraj that day, previously a righteous man, but zeal carried him - and said: You lie, by Allah, you shall not kill him, by Allah, nor can you kill him. So Usayd ibn Hudayr stood - he is the cousin of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh - and said to Sa'd ibn Ubadah: You lie, by Allah, we shall surely kill him; you are but a hypocrite arguing for the hypocrites. Then the two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, surged until they almost fought, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the pulpit; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept calming them until they quieted - or fell silent. She said: So I wept that day of mine, my tears never stopping nor sleeping with sleep, and my parents awoke with me, having wept my night, not sleeping with sleep nor my tears stopping, thinking weeping would split my liver. She said: While they sat with me and I wept, a woman of the Ansar sought permission upon me, so I permitted her and she sat weeping with me. While we were thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, greeted and sat - she said: He had not sat with me since what was said was said before it, having stayed a month without revelation. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testified then said: As for after, O Aishah, such-and-such reached me about you; if you are innocent, Allah will declare you innocent, and if you committed a sin, seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses his sin then repents to Allah, Allah turns to him. She said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his speech, my tears dried until I felt not a drop of them. So I said to my father: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for what he said. He said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah. So I said to my mother: Answer the Messenger of Allah for what he said. She said: I do not know how to answer the Messenger of Allah. I was a young girl not reading much of the Qur'an. So I said: By Allah, if I say I am innocent - and Allah knows I am innocent - you will not believe me in that; and if I confess a sin - and Allah knows I am innocent - you will believe me. By Allah, I find no example for me and you except Abu Yusuf's saying: {So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the One sought for help against what you describe}. She said: Then I turned and lay on my bed, she said: knowing then that I was innocent of it and that Allah, blessed and exalted, would declare me innocent with my innocence; but by Allah, I never thought Allah, blessed and exalted, would send down concerning my affair revelation to be recited - my affair in myself was too trifling for Allah to speak concerning me a matter to be recited - but I hoped the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would see in sleep a vision by which Allah would declare me innocent. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had not risen until revelation descended upon him, and he was seized by what used to seize him of heaviness, until sweat like pearls poured from him on a wintry day from the weight of the saying that descended upon him. When it was lifted from him, it was lifted while he laughed; the first word he spoke was: Rather, Allah has sent down your innocence. My mother said: Stand to the Messenger of Allah. I said: By Allah, I shall not stand to him, nor praise except Allah. She said: So Allah, mighty and exalted, revealed: {Indeed those who came with ifk are a group among you}, the ten verses all of them. She said: When Allah sent down this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr - who used to spend on Mistah for his kinship and his poverty - said: By Allah, I shall never spend on Mistah after what he said about Aishah. So Allah, mighty and exalted, revealed: {And let not those of virtue among you and affluence swear not to give} ... to His saying: {that Allah forgive you, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful}. Abu Bakr said: Yes, by Allah, I love that Allah forgive me. So he returned to Mistah the spending he used to spend on him, saying: By Allah, I shall never take it from him. Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had consulted Zaynab bint Jahsh in my affair, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I guard my hearing and sight; by Allah, I know only good. She said: So Allah preserved her with piety, while her sister perished among those who perished. al-Zuhri said: This is what reached us of the report of these men who narrated to me from Aishah."
"10243","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 154 / 130 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn Faraj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us from Yunus, from al-Zuhri who said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah informed him: that marriage in Jahiliyyah was of four kinds: one of them is the marriage of people today - a man proposes to a man for a woman, pays her dowry, then marries her. And another marriage: a man would say to his wife when she became pure from menstruation: Send to so-and-so, and her husband would keep away from her and never touch her until her pregnancy from that man became clear; when her pregnancy became clear, her husband would consummate with her. He only did that out of desire for a child, and this was called nikah. And a marriage: a group would gather and enter upon a woman, all of them having intercourse with her; when she conceived and gave birth, and nights passed after she gave birth, she would send to them, and no man among them could refrain until they gathered with her; she would say to them: You know what happened of your affair, and I have given birth, and he is your son or your daughter, O so-and-so. So she would name whomever she loved of them by his name, and he would become the child, accepting it; the man could not refrain. And the fourth marriage: people would gather and enter upon a woman who would not refuse whoever came to her - they are the prostitutes, who used to raise banners over their doors; whoever wanted them entered upon them - so when one of them conceived and gave birth, the physiognomists would be gathered for her, then they would attach the child to whom they saw, without refusal. Then when Allah sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth, He abolished the marriage of Jahiliyyah except the marriage of Islam. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10244","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 155 / 131 - Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us from Usamah ibn Zayd, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not speak speech in succession as you speak in succession, but he spoke distinct speech which everyone who heard it memorized. And this hadith was narrated by other than Zayd, from al-Thawri, from Usamah, from al-Qasim, from Aishah."
"10245","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 156 / 132 - I read to Muhammad ibn Mansur, saying: Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to you, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: This verse was revealed concerning Abdullah ibn Ubayy: {And he who took upon himself the greater part thereof}."
"10246","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 157 / 133 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Asbagh narrated to us from Ibn Wahb, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ma'afiri who informed him from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah that she said: When Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed: {And let them draw their khumur over their bosoms}, the first Muhajir women came and tore their murut and covered themselves with them. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah except Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"10247","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 158 / 134 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Uqayl narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fight on behalf of any of the polytheists except on behalf of the dhimmis. And we do not know anyone who corroborated Rishdin in this narration of his."
"10248","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 159 / 135 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, would lie down."
"10249","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 160 / 136 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Burd - meaning Ibn Sinan - narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: I sought to open the door while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, so he walked in his prayer - either to his right or to his left - until he opened for me. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Burd."
"10250","161 / 137 - Muhammad al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Burd narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah that she said: They claim that the prayer is cut off by a woman, a donkey and a dog; I saw myself before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his family bed, between him and the qiblah."
"10251","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 162 / 138 - Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some poetry is wisdom."
"10252","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 163 / 139 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Isa, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"10253","164 / 140 - And from Salim, from his father, they said: Concession was not granted for fasting the days of tashriq except for one detained (from sacrifice) or one performing tamattu'."
"10254","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 165 / 141 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he fell ill, would recite over himself with the mu'awwidhat and blow."
"10255","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 166 / 142 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven, making witr of them with one; when he finished his prayer he lay on his right side."
"10256","167 / 143 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The child belongs to the bed, and the adulterer gets the stone."
"10257","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 168 / 144 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and people prayed with his prayer, then the next night, then they gathered on the third or fourth night and became many, so he did not come out to them; in the morning he said: I saw what you did; nothing prevented me from coming out to you except fear it would be made obligatory upon you."
"10258","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 169 / 145 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The teacher of good - everything seeks forgiveness for him, even the fish in the sea."
"10259","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 170 / 146 - Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The seeker of knowledge - the angels spread their wings for him and seek forgiveness for him."
"10260","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 171 / 147 - Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, marfu' - he said: The death of a scholar is a breach in Islam, not closed as long as night and day differ. And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated from al-Zuhri and from Ibn al-Munkadir hadiths in which he was not corroborated, and we do not know anyone who narrated these hadiths other than him with this isnad."
"10261","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 172 / 148 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah who said: Quraysh satirized, so the Muslims came to Ka'b ibn Malik and said: Answer for us. He said: Seek permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they sought permission from the Messenger of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted, and he strove but did not reach. Then they came to Hassan ibn Thabit and called him; Hassan came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear you may satirize Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith. Hassan said: I shall surely draw you out of them as a hair is drawn from dough; I have a tongue - I would not love to have anyone's tongue in exchange - meaning: his tongue. Then he extended his tongue as if a bold serpent's tongue, with a black mole on its tip. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him, and he healed, satisfied and sufficed. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aishah with this wording except from this angle. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"10262","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 173 / 149 - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah who said: I entered upon Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz while he was governor over Madinah, with a group of his companions, and the scholars of the lands had gathered with him asking about this verse: {And if you fear you cannot do justice to orphans, marry what pleases you of women} up to: {And give women their dowries as a gift}. Urwah said: Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated to me that it was revealed concerning orphan girls among women orphans with men; a bad orphan girl would be with a man, possessing wealth, so he would neither marry her for her bad appearance nor leave her to marry until she died and he inherited her; if he married her he kept her unjustly without fulfilling her right to her. So Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed: {And if you fear you cannot do justice to orphans}, so leave them, do not marry them; {then marry what pleases you of women, two, three and four; if you fear you cannot be just, then one, or what your right hands possess; that is nearer that you not incline} - meaning: not incline; {And give women their dowries as an obligation}. Then after this verse was revealed: {And they ask you concerning women; say: Allah gives you verdict concerning them and what is recited to you in the Book concerning orphan girls to whom you do not give what is decreed for them while desiring to marry them}. So this other verse lightened. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her."
"10263","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 174 / 150 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pour over me from seven waterskins whose ties have not been loosened."
"10264","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 175 / 151 - Bishr ibn Adam ibn Bint Azhar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to sleep, he would join his hands, blow into them, then recite {Say: He is Allah, One} and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of people} and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak}, then wipe with them his face, head and rest of his body. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle from Aishah."
"10265","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 176 / 152 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: I knew my parents only as practicing the religion, and no day passed upon us except that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to us therein at both ends of the day, morning and evening. When the Muslims were tested, Abu Bakr left emigrating toward Abyssinia until, when he reached al-Ghimad, Ibn al-Daghinah met him and said: Where do you intend, O Abu Bakr? Abu Bakr said: My people expelled me, so I want to wander the earth and worship my Lord. Ibn al-Daghinah said: O Abu Bakr, one like you does not leave; you earn for the destitute, maintain kinship, bear the burden, honor the guest and help in calamities of truth. I am your protector, so return and worship your Lord in your town. So he returned, and Ibn al-Daghinah departed with him, going about the nobles of Quraysh in the evening, saying to them: One like Abu Bakr does not leave, nor does a man leave who earns for the destitute, maintains kinship, bears the burden, honors the guest and helps in calamities of truth. Quraysh did not dislike Ibn al-Daghinah's word, saying: Order Abu Bakr to worship his Lord in his house, praying therein, without harming us nor making it public, for we fear he may tempt our sons and women. Zayd ibn al-Daghinah said: He shall not make his prayer public nor recite outside his house. Then he told Abu Bakr what they said to him and what they returned upon him. So he took a mosque in his house's courtyard, reciting the Qur'an; the women and sons of the polytheists would pass by him looking at him, and he was a weeping man unable to hold his eyes when he recited the Qur'an. That frightened the nobles of Quraysh among the polytheists, so they sent to Ibn al-Daghinah saying: We sheltered Abu Bakr under your protection on condition he worship his Lord in his house, but he made prayer and recitation public, and we fear he may tempt our sons and women; he has violated - I think he said - what I contracted upon him, that he worship his Lord in his house, by returning your protection. Aishah said: So Ibn al-Daghinah came to Abu Bakr and said: You know what I covenanted for you; either do that - or a word like it - or return to me my protection, for I dislike Arabs talking that I was betrayed concerning a man I contracted for. Abu Bakr said: I have returned to you your protection. Abu Bakr prepared to emigrate, buying two mounts, feeding them leaves of samur - which is khabat - for four months. Ibn Shihab said: Urwah said: Aishah said: While we one day sat in Abu Bakr's house around noon, a speaker said to Abu Bakr: Here is the Messenger of Allah coming - I think he said: at an hour he did not used to come to us - so Abu Bakr said: By Allah, nothing brought him at this hour but a matter. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, sought permission, was permitted, and entered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: Remove those with you. Abu Bakr said: They are only your family, may my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah said: Permission has been given me to leave. Abu Bakr said: Companionship, may my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah said: Yes. Abu Bakr said: Then take, may my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, one of my two mounts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the price. Aishah said: So he took one of them; we prepared them and made for them provisions in a bag, and Asma cut one of her girdles and tied the bag's mouth with it - thence she was called Dhat al-Nitaq. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr went to a cave called Thawr; Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, a young lad, would spend the night with them, leaving from them at dawn to be with Quraysh in Makkah in the morning, hearing nothing but retaining it and bringing it to them, while Amir ibn Fuhayrah would pasture a milch flock for them, resting it upon them when an hour of the evening passed, doing that each night of those three nights. End of Urwah's hadith."
"10266","Abu Udhrah, from Aishah. Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 177 / 153 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Shaddad - a shaykh of Hammad's - from Abu Udhrah - who had reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade men and women from bathhouses, then permitted men in waist-wrappers. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from this angle."
"10267","Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah said: 178 / 154 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at night, so I followed him, and he came to al-Baqi' - or she said: the graveyard - and said: Peace be upon you, abodes of believing people; we shall surely join you. O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward nor tempt us after them."
"10268","Amr ibn Umayyah, from Aishah. Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 179 / 155 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to us from his father: that Umar came upon him in the market while he was bargaining for a cloak and said: What is this, O Amr? He said: A cloak I buy to give in charity. Umar said to him: Then you are you. Then he came upon him later and said: O Amr, what did the cloak do? He said: I gave it in charity? He said: To whom? He said: To a slave girl ......................... He said: Did you not claim you give it in charity? He said: Yes, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whatever you give them of anything, it is charity for you. He said: So Umar said: O Amr, do not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)!! He said: By Allah, I shall not leave you until you come to Umm al-Mu'minin Aishah. He said: O Amr, do not lie about the Messenger of Allah! So they sought permission upon Aishah, and Amr said: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whatever you give them is charity for you? She said: O Allah, yes; O Allah, yes. So Umar said: Where was I of this? Business in the markets distracted me."
"10269","Abu Umamah ibn Sahl. Ahmad narrated to us, he said: 180 / 156 - Muhammad ibn Nasih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Uthmah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us - in my view: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz - he said: Umayyah ibn Hind narrated to me from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl who said: I entered, I and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, upon Aishah, and Aishah informed us: that a poor man came to the door while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat, so I ordered a woman with me to hand him something; when she took it to hand the poor man, I said: Bring it so I may look. He said: O Aishah, does nothing go out except with your knowledge? I said: Nothing goes out except with my knowledge. He said: Do not withhold, lest Allah withhold from you. And we do not know that Abu Umamah narrated with an isnad from Aishah except this hadith, and it has another path from Abu Umamah."
"10270","Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from Aishah. Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: 181 / 157 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Qatadah, from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed six rak'ahs in four prostrations - meaning: in the eclipse."
"10271","182 / 158 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Ata, from Ubayd, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never more strict in observing supererogatory glorification (prayer) than his observing the two rak'ahs - I think she said: the two rak'ahs after Zuhr."
"10272","183 / 159 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr who said: Aishah informed me that she said to the players: I wished to see them. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and I stood at the door looking between his ear and shoulder while they played in the mosque."
"10273","184 / 160 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj who said: Ata narrated to me, he said: Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to me, he said: One I believe - meaning Aishah - narrated to me, he said: The sun eclipsed, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with people in a long standing, then bowed and prostrated, saying when he bowed: Allah is Greatest, and when he raised his head: Allah hears him who praises Him. Then he prayed therein six rak'ahs until men almost fainted, until skins of water were poured upon them. When the sun cleared, he addressed us, praising Allah and extolling Him, then said: The sun and moon are not eclipsed for anyone's death nor life, but they are two signs among Allah's signs by which He frightens His servants; whichever of them eclipses, pray until it clears. And he prayed with them until it cleared."
"10274","185 / 161 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until what he wished of women was made lawful for him. He said: I said: Who informed you? He said: I think Ubayd ibn Umayr."
"10275","186 / 161 (m) - Ibn Jurayj said: And Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard a man narrating it to Ata from Ubayd ibn Umayr."
"10276","187 / 162 - And Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until what he wished of women was made lawful for him."
"10277","188 / 163 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Killing a Muslim is not lawful except in three cases: an adulterer, married, so he is stoned; a man who kills deliberately, so he is killed for it; and a man who leaves Islam, so he is killed."
"10278","189 / 164 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10279","190 / 165 - And Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory."
"10280","191 / 166 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah who said: I used to wash, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel."
"10281","192 / 167 - Amr narrated it to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Qurrah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah who said: I used to wash, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, both drawing from it together; I would do no more than pour three handfuls over my head."
"10282","193 / 168 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad and Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata claimed he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr saying: I heard Aishah claiming that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stay with Zaynab bint Jahsh and drink honey with her, so I and Hafsah agreed that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, she should say: I smell from you the odor of maghafir; have you eaten maghafir? So he entered upon one of them, and she said that to him. He said: No, rather I drank honey with Zaynab bint Jahsh, and I shall never return to it. So was revealed: {O Prophet, why do you prohibit what Allah made lawful for you} to His saying: {And when the Prophet confided to one of his wives}, his saying: Rather I drank honey. And we do not know a path for this hadith from Aishah better than this path, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Jurayj except Hajjaj ibn Muhammad."
"10283","194 / 169 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs narrated to us from his father, from al-A'mash, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from al-Qasim, from Aishah - the like of it."
"10284","195 / 170 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Aishah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, {And those who give what they give} - or he said: [{And those who give what they give}] {while their hearts fear}."
"10285","196 / 171 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah ibn Jud'an used to honor the guest, maintain kinship and do deeds; will that benefit him? He said: No, for he never once said: Forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment."
"10286","Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah. 197 / 172 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: When was revealed: {Of it are verses precise, they are the mother of the Book, and others unspecific; as for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is unspecific of it}, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see those who dispute concerning it, they are those whom Allah, blessed and exalted, meant, so beware of them."
"10287","198 / 173 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: He said: My father narrated to me from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it. And this hadith was thus narrated by Ayyub, Ali ibn Zayd and Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah. And Hammad ibn Salamah and Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Qasim, from Aishah."
"10288","199 / 174 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is scrutinized in reckoning is punished. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, does not Allah, blessed and exalted, say: {Then he shall be reckoned with an easy reckoning}? He said: That is the presentation, and whoever is scrutinized in reckoning is punished. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah."
"10289","200 / 175 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, the most eminent of those who narrated it being Ayyub."
"10290","201 / 176 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that some Jews passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: al-Sam (death). So he said: Upon you. I said: Rather upon you be al-Sam and the curse. He said: O Aishah, did you not hear me return it upon them? Allah loves gentleness."
"10291","202 / 177 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Sahl al-Sarraj narrated to us from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken between my breast and throat, in my house and on my day. And this hadith was narrated from Ibn Abi Mulaykah by more than one, and from Ayyub by other than Sahl; we mentioned it from Sahl only for the rarity of Sahl's hadith, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sahl except Abu Asim."
"10292","203 / 178 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: No character was more hateful to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than lying; when he learned of something of that from anyone, it would leave his heart until he knew he had renewed repentance. And this hadith was narrated by Ma'mar from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah. And Hammad ibn Zayd and Hatim ibn Wardan narrated it from Ayyub, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Aishah."
"10293","204 / 179 - Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Ma'qil ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la narrated to us from Ayyub, and Isl - meaning Ibn Sufyan - from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an melodiously."
"10294","205 / 180 - And Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Sadusi narrated it to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Isl, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an melodiously. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh and Rawh, nor do we know that Shu'bah narrated with an isnad from Isl except this hadith. And there is disagreement over Ibn Abi Mulaykah in this narration: Amr ibn Dinar narrated from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abi Nahik, from Sa'd. And al-Layth narrated it likewise as Amr narrated, except that he differed in his name. And Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas. And Nafi' ibn Umar narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn al-Zubayr. And Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abi Yazid, from Abu Lubabah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10295","206 / 181 - Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: When I was accused of what I was accused of, I wanted to throw myself into a well."
"10296","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah."
"10297","And from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abd al-Rahman to perform Umrah with Aishah - I think he said: from al-Tanim. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, except Hammad ibn Zayd. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except Yunus."
"10298","And Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated it to us, he said: al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abd al-Rahman to perform Umrah with her from al-Tanim."
"10299","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Bakkar, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he cursed - or a word like it - those who imitate Allah's creation. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, except Wuhayb. And none narrated it from Wuhayb except Sahl."
"10300","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: There was no character more hateful to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than lying; and a man would tell a lie in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it would continue to weigh against him in himself, until he knew that he had repented from it."
"10301","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: It reached Aishah that a woman wore sandals, so Aishah said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed masculine women. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, except Ibn Uyaynah."
"10302","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the most hateful of men to Allah is the fiercely hostile disputant."
"10303","Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of sacrifices, then he permitted it; and he forbade visiting graves, then he permitted it - I think he said: for it reminds of the Hereafter."
"10304","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, reciting at night, and said: Praise be to Allah who has placed in my Ummah one like him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Usamah, and we heard it only from al-Fadl, from al-Walid ibn Salih, from Abu Usamah."
"10305","Abdullah ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he saw a cloud portending rain, his face would change; and when it rained, his face would brighten. And this hadith, thus did the companions of Ibn Jurayj narrate it, from Ata, from Aishah, except Abu Muawiyah, for he narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah."
"10306","Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram, I perfumed him with the best of my perfume."
"10307","And Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the month is twenty-nine days. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, except Abu Amir al-Khazzaz."
"10308","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the son of the sister of a people is from them. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah except through this route, and none narrated it from Abu Amir except Attab ibn Harb."
"10309","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a woman suffering prolonged bleeding: Perform ghusl and ablution for every prayer."
"10310","Ahmad ibn Ishaq and Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muammil narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The quickest of people to perish are your people. I said: Why? May Allah make me your ransom. He said: Indeed this tribe of Quraysh - deaths find them sweet, and people envy them. I said: Then what remains of people after them? He said: They are the backbone of people; when they perish, people perish. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah with this wording except through this route."
"10311","Abu Ubaydah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muammil narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent condiment vinegar is. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Ibn al-Muammil, nor from Abdullah ibn al-Muammil except Zayd ibn al-Hubab."
"10312","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Hakkam ibn Salm narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will not sanctify a nation in which the right of the weak is not taken from the strong. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah except through this route."
"10313","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muammil narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his bed, and I thought he had gone to one of his wives; then I found him: he had risen quickly and taken his cloak upon his shoulder, so I took my waist-wrapper. I said: What is he doing? He went out and I went out behind him; whenever he hastened, I hastened, until he came to al-Baqi, where he raised his hands supplicating three times, then he turned back and hastened, and I hastened, until I entered the house and he entered after me, and he said: What is the matter with you? Did you fear that Allah and His Messenger would wrong you? Jibril came to me and commanded me to come to the people of al-Baqi and seek forgiveness for them."
"10314","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muammil narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a lamp in the house of al-Zubayr and said: O Aishah, I think Asma has given birth; so do not name him until I name him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and named him and rubbed his palate with a date. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah except through this route."
"10315","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Alqamah informed us, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that Jibril brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) her image in a green cloth, and said: O Muhammad, this is your wife in this world and the Hereafter. And this hadith, thus Abd al-Razzaq narrated it; and Isa ibn Yunus narrated it, from Abdullah ibn Alqamah, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah."
"10316","Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, he said: I said to Aishah: O Mother of the Believers, a man divorced his wife three times, then she married another man, then she cast her veil before him and then he divorced her - is she lawful for the first husband? She said: O son of my sister, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about the like of what you asked me, and he said: She is not lawful for the other until he tastes of her honey."
"10317","Amr ibn Abdullah al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi al-Sufayra - and he is Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik - narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from me cheerful and in good spirits, and returned grieving. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you went out from me cheerful and in good spirits, and returned grieving! He said: Indeed I entered the Kabah, and I wish I had not entered - or: I had not done it - indeed I fear that I have burdened my Ummah. And this hadith, we do not know for it any route except this route."
"10318","Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me and saw meat, and said: Who sent this? I said: Uthman. She said: Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands supplicating for Uthman. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Aishah except Ibn Abi Mulaykah, nor from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik."
"10319","Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them; and from the meat of sacrifices - I think he said: that they keep it - so eat. Or: she said: so he permitted it for them. And we do not know that Abu al-Tayyah narrated from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, except this hadith; nor did anyone narrate it from Abu al-Tayyah except Bistam ibn Muslim, a shaykh from Basra, well known; Shubah and others narrated from him."
"10320","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Bakkar ibn Abdullah informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating from Aishah, she said: We had a singing girl with us; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while she was in that state, then Umar sought permission and she jumped up. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, so I said: What are you laughing at, O Messenger of Allah? He informed him, and he said: I will not leave until I hear what you hear - or: what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard from him - so he commanded her and she let him hear. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Bakkar ibn Abdullah, nor from Bakkar except Abd al-Razzaq."
"10321","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulaym - and he is a man from Makkah - narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves from the Fire even with half a date. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah except through this route with this isnad; and Muhammad ibn Sulaym narrated this hadith; Waki and Abu Asim narrated it from him."
"10322","Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding this verse: {He it is who sent down upon you the Book; in it are verses precise - they are the foundation of the Book - and others ambiguous}, and he said: When you see those who follow what is ambiguous thereof, they are those, so beware of them. And we do not know that Muhammad ibn Sulaym ascribed except these two hadiths."
"10323","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us - and the wording is Ibrahim's - they said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: When the pain of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intensified, he said: Bring me an inkpot and a shoulder-blade - or a paper - I will write for Abu Bakr a document over which people will not differ. Then he said: Allah forbid that people differ over Abu Bakr. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay except Muhammad ibn Aban."
"10324","Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Yala narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah and Ikrimah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to a pot and took a bone with meat from it, ate, then went to prayer and did not perform ablution, but rinsed his mouth."
"10325","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the boy, two equivalent sheep - I think he said: and for the girl, a sheep. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward."
"10326","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you."
"10327","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"10328","Muhammad ibn Firas Abu Hurayrah al-Sayrafi, Yahya ibn Hakim, and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, they said: Harami ibn Umarah informed us, he said: al-Harish ibn al-Khirrit narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: Three covered vessels would be placed for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night: a vessel for his purification, a vessel for his drink, and a vessel for his siwak. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Aishah, and we do not know for it any isnad from Aishah except this isnad."
"10329","Yahya ibn Hakim and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, they said: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: al-Harish ibn al-Khirrit narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: In tayammum there are two strikes: a strike for the face, and a strike for the hands up to the elbows. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah except through this route; and al-Harish is a man from Basra, the brother of al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit."
"10330","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Uthman ibn al-Aswad except Abu Asim. And some of the companions of Abu Asim narrated it from Abu Asim, from Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah - mursal. And more than one ascribed it."
"10331","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah and Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is closely questioned about the reckoning will perish. I said: O Messenger of Allah, {As for he who is given his record in his right hand, he will be reckoned an easy reckoning}?! He said: That is the presentation."
"10332","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while I was in front of him."
"10333","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub in Ramadan from other than a wet dream, then he would bathe and fast."
"10334","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, Aishah said: I perfumed him with the best perfume I could, may my father and mother be his ransom, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10335","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never came to me after Asr except he prayed two rakahs."
"10336","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a cloud portending rain, his face would change, and he would turn forward and back; and when it rained, it was relieved from him. I mentioned that to him, and he said: I am not safe that it be as He said: {Then when they saw it as a cloud approaching their valleys}."
"10337","Amr ibn Ali and Ahmad ibn al-Wazir narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah and His Messenger are the patron of one who has no patron, and the maternal uncle is the heir of one who has no heir. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who ascribed it from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Asim. And the two hadiths of Tawus, we do not know anyone who narrated them from Tawus except Mamar."
"10338","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Sulayman - meaning al-Amash - from Mujahid, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the dead, for they have gone forth to what they sent ahead."
"10339","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash and Layth, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: A man entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he turned to him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this not so-and-so? He said: Indeed the worst of people in rank is one whom people avoid because of his obscenity."
"10340","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he brought him near and close; when he went out, I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this not so-and-so whose evil you used to mention? He said: Yes. I said: You treated him gently - or: you brought him near - and drew his seat close. He said: Indeed the worst of people are those who are honored out of fear of their evil. And this hadith has been narrated from Aishah through various routes; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Aishah, except Sharik."
"10341","Abd al-Ala ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Aishah: that Safiyyah menstruated, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is she detaining us? They said: O Messenger of Allah, she has circumambulated the House at the Ifadah. He said: Then let her depart. And we do not know that Ibn Abi Najih narrated from Mujahid, from Aishah, except this hadith."
"10342","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Sibghi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Aishah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were in ihram, and caravans would pass by; when they drew near us, we would let down over our faces a portion of our headscarves."
"10343","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad and Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: I saw the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Layth and Yazid except Ali ibn Asim, who combined them."
"10344","Muhammad ibn Salih al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Aishah, he raised it, he said: When the sins of the servant increase and he finds nothing to expiate them, Allah afflicts him with grief to expiate his sins thereby. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Layth, from Mujahid, from Aishah, except Zaidah; nor from Zaidah except Husayn ibn Ali."
"10345","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from his father, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: We had a wild animal; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present, it would stay still and remain in its place, neither coming nor going; and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, it would come and go."
"10346","Al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Baghdadi and Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Abu Husayn, from Mujahid, from Aishah: that when her exoneration was revealed, Abu Bakr kissed her head, and she said: Will you not exonerate me? He said: What heaven would shade me or what earth would carry me if I said what I do not know."
"10347","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir. And this hadith, Zubayd narrated it from Mujahid, from Aishah; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Zubayd except al-Thawri. And Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated it from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah. And Bashir Abu Ismail narrated it from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr."
"10348","Ammar ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: Washing the woman's private part is from the Sunnah."
"10349","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Mihja narrated to us, he said: Qazah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih and Humayd al-Araj..."
"10350","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Said al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and intends good thereby, Allah will appoint for him a righteous minister: if he forgets, he reminds him; and if he remembers, he helps him."
"10351","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while I lay across in front of him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya, from Amrah, from Aishah, except Faraj ibn Fadalah, and he was not a memorizer."
"10352","Al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the hadith of Yahya, from Amrah, except al-Layth; nor from Layth except Yahya ibn Hassan; and we heard it only from al-Hasan, and he was trustworthy and reliable."
"10353","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, he said: It was said to her: What would the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do in his house? She said: He would mend his sandal and sew his garment. And this hadith, al-Layth narrated it thus from Muawiyah, from Yahya, from Amrah, from Aishah. And Hammad ibn Khalid narrated it from Muawiyah, from Yahya, from al-Qasim, from Aishah. And Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated it from Yahya ibn Said, from Humayd al-Makki, from Mujahid, from Aishah. And Ibn Jurayj narrated it from Yahya ibn Said, from Mujahid, from Aishah."
"10354","Umar ibn al-Khattab and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, they said: Said ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Souls are marshalled hosts. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya, from Amrah, except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"10355","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Witr, in the first rakah, {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, and in the second, {Say: O disbelievers}, and in the third, {Say: He is Allah, One}."
"10356","Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Kathir ibn Ufayr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, she said: I asked Aishah: What would the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Witr? She said: He would recite in the two rakahs after which he performs Witr, in the first of them {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, and in the second {Say: O disbelievers}, with taslim; and he would recite in the rakah in which he performs Witr {Say: He is Allah, One}, and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak}, and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind}."
"10357","Muhammad ibn al-Ala Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to observe itikaf, he would pray Fajr then enter his place of seclusion; and when he intended to observe itikaf in the last ten of Ramadan, he ordered his tent and it was pitched; then when he prayed Fajr, he looked and the tents had been pitched."
"10358","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, that she was asked about ghusl on Friday, and she said: People used to work for themselves, so it was said to them: If only you would bathe - and I think in the hadith: they would come in the evening in their states, so it was said to them: If only you would bathe."
"10359","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Abu Bakr came in to me while a Jewish woman was performing ruqyah on me, and he said: Perform ruqyah on her with the Book of Allah. And a Jewish woman came and I gave her a piece of bread, and she said: May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in and I informed him of her words, and he said: The punishment of the grave is true. I never saw him after that offer a prayer except he sought refuge in it from the punishment of the grave."
"10360","Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - similar to it."
"10361","And Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Tai narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - similar to it. He said: I never saw him after that offer a prayer except he sought refuge in it from the punishment of the grave. And the hadith of al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, we do not know anyone who ascribed it from him except Zayd ibn al-Hubab. And the hadith of Shubah, we do not know anyone who ascribed it except Muhammad ibn Bakr."
"10362","Ubayd ibn Ismail al-Habbari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed four rakahs in the eclipse. And this hadith has been narrated from Aishah through various routes regarding the eclipse; and we do not know anyone who said: from Aishah that he prayed four rakahs, except Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah."
"10363","Abdullah ibn Said Abu Said al-Kindi al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: When Jafar was announced dead, it was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If only you forbade wailing? He said - I think he said to a man: Go to them and forbid them. He said: I went, and they did not obey me; then a second time, then a third; then he said: Go back to them and throw dust in their faces. - And I was peeking through the crack of the door - so I said to the man: May Allah abase your nose; by Allah, you neither left the Messenger of Allah nor did you do - meaning: what he commanded him, that he throw dust in their faces. And this hadith, Abu Khalid and Said ibn Maslamah narrated it from Yahya, from Amrah, from Aishah. And others narrated it with other than this isnad from Yahya ibn Said."
"10364","Yahya ibn al-Mualla ibn Mansur and Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I used to play with dolls, and my girl companions would come to me, but they would hold back; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, he would send them to me."
"10365","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The quickest of you to join me is the longest of you in hand; so they would stretch to see which of them was longest in hand."
"10366","Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Said, he said: Amrah informed me that she heard Aishah say: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with five nights remaining of Dhu al-Qadah, seeing nothing but Hajj, until when we drew near Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded whoever did not have a sacrificial animal with him, when he circumambulated the House, to exit ihram. Then on the Day of Sacrifice, meat was brought in to us, and I said: What is this? It was said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed cattle on behalf of his wives. Yahya said: So I met al-Qasim and narrated to him, and he said: By Allah, she brought you the hadith correctly."
"10367","Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I would comb the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in itikaf, and he would not enter the house except for a need - or: for human need - and he would incline his head to me and I would comb it while he was in itikaf."
"10368","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Ammar ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah - and once he said: that Umarah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah - narrated to him, from Muhammad ibn Muslim - meaning al-Zuhri - that Urwah narrated to him from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then sell her even for a rope. And al-dafir is the rope. And this hadith, its isnad has been differed over in the narration of al-Zuhri: a group narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid. And Ibn Uyaynah said: from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid and Shibl ibn Mabad. And Uqayl, Yunus, and al-Zubaydi narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Shibl ibn Khulayd, from Abdullah ibn Malik al-Awsi."
"10369","Khalaf ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cutting is for a quarter dinar and above."
"10370","And I heard Ibrahim ibn Said say: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: We memorized it from four: from al-Zuhri, Yahya ibn Said, Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, and Ruzayq ibn Hakim, each narrating it from Amrah, from Aishah; three of them stopped it, and al-Zuhri raised it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Cutting is for a quarter dinar and above."
"10371","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah or Urwah, from Aishah - thus Ibn Uyaynah said - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I entered Paradise and heard recitation in it, and I said: Who is this? It was said: Harithah ibn al-Numan. Thus is righteousness, thus is righteousness. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Aishah with this isnad."
"10372","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah - or Urwah - from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of Abu Musa reciting and said: This one has indeed been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah except through this route with this isnad."
"10373","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Samurah and Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would treat the sick with ruqyah, placing his finger on the ground, saying: By the soil of our land and the saliva of one of us, our sick is healed by the permission of our Lord. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this isnad; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd Rabbihi except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, and we do not know anyone who narrated from Abd Rabbihi, from Amrah, from Aishah, except this hadith."
"10374","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Said narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Breaking the bone of the dead is like breaking it alive. And Yahya ibn Said, Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, and Sad ibn Said are brothers; the most reliable of them is Yahya."
"10375","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar - meaning al-Mukharrimi - narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn al-Had narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The hand is cut for a quarter dinar and above. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Amrah, from Aishah, except Yazid ibn al-Had."
"10376","Al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah cursed the briber and the bribed. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Aishah except through this route; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Bakr except Ishaq ibn Yahya, and he is weak in hadith; yet a group of scholars narrated from him, among them Ibn al-Mubarak and others."
"10377","Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands before he performed Ifadah."
"10378","And Muhammad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of that."
"10379","Muhammad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Aflah ibn Abi al-Quays came to me seeking permission after the veil had been imposed upon me, and I turned him away; and he was my uncle through suckling. She said: I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It would not have harmed you to permit him; indeed he is your uncle. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, only the woman suckled me, the man did not suckle me. He said: Indeed he is your uncle. She said: Aishah used to say: Indeed suckling makes unlawful what birth makes unlawful."
"10380","Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from Amrah, from Aishah, the like of that. Meaning: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10381","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: We did not know of the burial of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we heard the sound of shovels at the end of the night."
"10382","Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Ibrahim, son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died when he was eighteen months old, and funeral prayer was not offered over him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Aishah with this wording."
"10383","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, that she said: We continued to hear of Isaf and Nailah: a man and a woman of Jurhum who committed adultery in the Kabah, and were transformed into two stones. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Aishah with this isnad."
"10384","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that she said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw of women what we see, he would have prevented them as the women of the Children of Israel were prevented. I saw us praying Fajr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in our cloaks, and none of us recognized the faces of others."
"10385","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ubaydullah - meaning Ibn Umar - from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) partitioned with a mat, and would pray; people began praying behind him, then he said: O people, upon you is what you can bear of deeds; for Allah will not tire until you tire; and know that the most beloved deeds to Allah are the most constant, even if little. And we do not know that Ubaydullah ascribed from Amrah, from Aishah, except these two hadiths."
"10386","Yahya ibn Ward ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah: that men complained of women to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he permitted them to strike them; then that night many women went about, and she said: The women of the Muslims have suffered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Strike them, but the best of you will not strike - I think he said. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah except through this route with this isnad."
"10387","Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah."
"10388","And from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The verse of stoning and suckling was revealed, and they were in a sheet beneath my bed; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, we were preoccupied with his death, and a tame animal entered and ate it."
"10389","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Asad ibn Zurarah, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I saw the leader of the elephant and its driver, blind and crippled, begging in Makkah."
"10390","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu Said al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to me, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Hafsa and I woke fasting voluntarily, then a gift was presented to us and we ate from it; Hafsa hastened to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Fast a day in its place. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who corroborated Jarir ibn Hazim in his narration, nor anyone who corroborated Ibn Wahb in his narration from Jarir. And Hammad ibn Zayd narrated it from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, he said: It reached me that Aishah and Hafsa... And what Hammad ibn Zayd narrated is the preserved from Yahya ibn Said."
"10391","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Harithah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began prayer, would say takbir then say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god but You. And this hadith, Harithah narrated it from Amrah, from Aishah. And Malik ibn Mighwal also narrated it from Ata, from Aishah."
"10392","Muhammad ibn Umarah narrated it to us, he said: Sahl ibn Amir narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Ata, he said: Ubayd ibn Umayr and I entered upon Aishah, and she mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - regarding the opening of prayer - similar to what Harithah narrated from Amrah, from Aishah."
"10393","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Thana: Shuja ibn al-Walid, he said: Harithah informed us, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no zakat in wealth until a year passes over it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this isnad."
"10394","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Shuja narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Muhammad, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surplus water is not withheld, nor the benefit of a well. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Aishah except from the hadith of Amrah, from Aishah."
"10395","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Shuja narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Muhammad, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who feigns satiety with what he was not given - or: attains - is like one wearing two garments of falsehood."
"10396","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Muhammad, from Amrah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began ablution, would mention the name."
"10397","Ibrahim ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Rijal - meaning Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman - narrated to us, from his father, from Amrah, from Aishah, from the Prophet, upon him peace: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him say good or be silent; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest."
"10398","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from his father, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave two rakahs after Asr. And Harithah ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman are lenient in hadith."
"10399","Umar ibn al-Khattab - as I think - and Muhammad ibn Idris narrated to us, they said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Abu al-Aswad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: He had commanded them not to eat sacrificial meat beyond three days, then he permitted - I think he said: for them. And we do not know that Hisham ibn Urwah narrated from Yahya ibn Said except this hadith, nor that Abu al-Aswad narrated from Hisham except this hadith."
"10400","Ismail ibn Abi Ismail al-Basri and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, they said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives: The longest of you in hand will follow me. Aishah said: When we would gather in the house of one of us after the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would stretch our hands along the wall to see who was longest; we continued to do that until Zaynab bint Jahsh ibn Riab, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died; and she was a short woman and was not the longest of us; then we knew that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) meant charity by length of hand. She said: Zaynab was a craftswoman; she would work and sew - meaning: she used to work - and give charity in the path of Allah. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya, from Amrah, from Aishah, except Abu Uways."
"10401","Ismail ibn Abi Ismail and Abdullah ibn Abi Shabib narrated to us, they said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman. And from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: I marvel at one who eats the crow, though the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the muhrim to kill it and called it wicked; by Allah, it is not of the good things."
"10402","Ismail ibn Abi Ismail al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out in the depth of the night to Baqi al-Gharqad and supplicate for its people; she said: Perhaps he did that more than once in a single night. And this hadith, others than Abu Uways narrated it from Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Aishah."
"10403","Said ibn Bahr al-Qirtasi narrated to us, he said: Man ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: Women would attend Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wrapped in their cloaks, unrecognized due to the darkness."
"10404","Ubayd ibn Ismail al-Habbari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham - meaning Ibn Urwah - from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Unlawful by suckling is what is unlawful by birth. And we do not know that Hisham ibn Urwah ascribed from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, except this hadith."
"10405","Muammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim - and he is Ibn Ulayyah - narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray sitting; when he intended to bow, he would stand for as long as a man reads - I think he said: forty verses. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Amrah, from Aishah, except al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham. And he is a man from Basra; he narrated from Juwayriyah ibn Asma and Ismail ibn Ibrahim. And his brother is Hisham. And Abu Hisham's name is Ziyad."
"10406","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Uways, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in and heard the voice of a boy, and said: What is with your boy crying; will you not seek ruqyah for him against the evil eye. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr except Abu Uways."
"10407","Al-Harith ibn al-Khidr al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah daughter of Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The people of Jahiliyyah would dye cotton on the day of Aqiqah, then shave the boy and place it on his head; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to place khaluq in place of blood."
"10408","Abu Umar Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mufarrij narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah: that she wanted to buy Barirah, but they stipulated her wala; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Buy her and free her, for wala belongs to the one who frees. And meat was brought and it was said to him: This is from what was given in charity to Barirah; he said: It is charity for her and a gift for us. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice, and her husband was free."
"10409","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to sleep or eat while junub, he would perform ablution as for prayer."
"10410","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought food from a Jew on credit and gave him his armor as a pledge."
"10411","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the best what a man eats is from his earning, and indeed his child is from his earning."
"10412","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Safiyyah, and we said: She has menstruated. He said: Aqra - or: Halqa - I see her but detaining us; we said: She circumambulated on the Day of Sacrifice. He said: Then no; order her to depart."
"10413","Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar and Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"10414","Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: I asked Aishah: How would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act among his family? She said: He would be in the service of his family; when prayer came, he stood for prayer."
"10415","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: People say that prayer is cut off by the dog, the donkey, and the woman; I would often see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying at night while I was between him and the qiblah; when I needed something, I would slip away from the side of the bed's legs, disliking..."
